From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:59:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] wifi: ath12k: Add opt-in cold boot calibration for PCI
 devices

Qualcomm's downstream cnss2 driver runs a cold boot calibration (CBC)
on WCN7850-family chips when the platform sets qcom,wlan-cbc-enabled,
as the Kaanapali (SM8850) devices do: the firmware first boots in
calibration mode (wlan mode 7), writes its RF calibration into the
CALDB memory region and sends a COLD_BOOT_CAL_DONE indication (QMI
0x003E); the device is then power cycled and boots into mission mode
with cal_done set in the host capabilities, so the firmware uses that
calibration instead of calibrating at run time. ath12k never does this.

Add it behind a new module parameter, ath12k.cold_boot_cal, default
off, so that the behaviour of every device stays as it is unless the
user opts in, and the effect can be compared without another build:

- on the first FW_READY of a PCI device, with the parameter set and
  calibration not yet done or tried, send the calibration mode instead
  of continuing into mission mode;
- on COLD_BOOT_CAL_DONE set qmi.cal_done and, from a work item, set the
  firmware mode OFF and power cycle the device through the HIF. The
  target memory chunks, CALDB included, are reused across the power
  cycle because their type and size do not change;
- if the indication does not come within 30 s, power cycle into mission
  mode without the calibration; a failed mode request continues without
  it at once. The calibration is tried once per device probe.

After a calibration-only boot MHI is up but the HIF was never started,
so ath12k_pci_power_down() would return early; let it power down while
a calibration is running. The work is cancelled on PCI remove.

The parameter is read at the first firmware ready, so it can be changed
at run time for the next probe (unbind / bind or module reload).

Inspired by Reixo's "wifi: ath12k: Add support for the peach (WCN7880)
chip" (Reixo0/nx809j-mainline, patch 0017), which implemented the
calibration flow for the same chip (PCI 17cb:110e) and measured about
8 s for the calibration; this is a re-implementation of only the
calibration part, as an opt-in switch for the existing WCN7850-family
support, with a timeout and a single attempt per probe.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
